    <commands><command>
                        <name>Siemens.OpcenterEX.PR.OperationalData.EquipAllocation_OP.OPModel.Commands.AllocateEquipmentFromTask</name>
                        <shortname>AllocateEquipmentFromTask</shortname>
                        <description>The command will allocate Equipment to the Work Order related to the given task. The command performs the folllowing checks: 1. if the given Task exist, if not error 11613 is returned; 2. if the Work Order Context related to the Task exists, if not error 11700 is returned; 3. if the Task Parameter with NId "EquipmentToAllocate" exists, if not error 11702 is returned. If the Task is configured to allocate equipment through a Work Order Operation Equipment Requirement: 1. if the Task Parameter with NId "RequirementTag" exists, if not error 11702 is returned; 2. if the execution of the command GetWorkOrderOperationEquipmentRequirementsFromTags succeed, if not error 11709 is returned; 3. if the command GetWorkOrderOperationEquipmentRequirementsFromTags returns a Work Order Operation Equipment Requirement, if not error 11703 is returned. Then the command checks: 1. if the piece of Equipment identify by the Task Parameter with NId "EquipmentToAllocate" exists, if not error 11706 is returned; 2. if the Equipment facet Equipment Allocation Properties exists, if not error 11707 is returned. If the piece of Equipment to allocated is already allocated to the same entity: 1. if the Task Context "EquipmentAllocationTaskContextDefinition" exists, if not error 11707 is returned; 2. if the Task Context User Field "AllowAllocationToSameEntity" exists, if not error 11707 is returned; 3. if the value of the Task Context User Field "AllowAllocationToSameEntity" is set to true, if not error 11708 is returned. Then the command checks: 1. if the execution of the command AllocateEquipment succeed, if not error 11704 is returned; 2. if the Task Parameter with NId "AllocatedEquipment" exists, if not error 11702 is returned; 3. if the execution of the command UpdateTaskParameter succeed, if not error 11705 is returned.</description>
                        <assembly>Siemens.OpcenterEX.PR.OperationalData.EquipAllocation_OP.OPModel.Commands, Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null</assembly>
                        <dotnetcommandtype></dotnetcommandtype>
                        <commandtype>Undefined</commandtype>
                        <domain>OperationalData</domain>
                        <visibility>Protected</visibility>
                        <composite>false</composite>
