                        <name>Siemens.OpcenterEX.PR.OperationalData.EquipAllocation_OP.OPModel.Commands.ReleaseEquipmentFromTask</name>
                        <shortname>ReleaseEquipmentFromTask</shortname>
                        <description>The command will release the allocated Equipment related to this task. The command performs the folllowing checks: 1. if the given Task exist, if not error 11613 is returned; 2. if the Work Order Context related to the Task exists, if not error 11700 is returned; 3. if the Task Parameter with NId "EquipmentToRelease" exists, if not error 11702 is returned; 4. if the value of the Task Parameter with NId "EquipmentToRelease" is not empty, if not error 11711 is returned; 5. if the piece of Equipment identify by the Task Parameter with NId "EquipmentToRelease" exists, if not error 11706 is returned; 6. if the execution of the command ReleaseEquipment succeed, if not error 11710 is returned; 7. if the Task Parameter with NId "ReleasedEquipment" exists, if not error 11702 is returned; 8. if the execution of the command UpdateTaskParameter succeed, if nor error 11705 is returned.</description>
